1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:10,691
I am the blacksmith. I run the analysis: I load your data, compute what you ask for, train and test models, and build small apps to explore the results.

2
00:00:11,099 --> 00:00:23,392
I load your data tables, such as CSV and Excel files, compute the features and statistics you ask for, and train and evaluate classifiers. I build interactive apps so you can explore a dataset.

3
00:00:23,392 --> 00:00:34,358
What makes me different: I run the computation itself on your data, and leave the commented code beside the result, so anyone can repeat it.

4
00:00:34,749 --> 00:00:45,463
I cover the computing: data, statistics, models and apps. I leave the commented code beside each result, so the adversary can run it again and check the method.

5
00:00:45,463 --> 00:00:53,271
I read your original data and leave it untouched. Each new result goes in a new, numbered file.

6
00:00:53,649 --> 00:01:04,270
A real run, on simulated data. Growth medium turned out to be mixed up with country, so the member asks me for the serum effect within each country, with a matching test.

7
00:01:04,270 --> 00:01:14,140
My answer is Done. The effect holds, but the countries disagree, and I say so. I save the results and the code that made them.

8
00:01:14,549 --> 00:01:24,055
Say what you want built: an app to explore your quality control, a classifier tested the way your data demand, or a series of steps on a counts table.

9
00:01:24,055 --> 00:01:30,856
I work in Python by default; name a template script in your request and I follow it.

10
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:39,687
To use me, type to Claude Code and name me: ask the blacksmith to compute, train or build something. Tell me which data, and what you want out.

11
00:01:39,687 --> 00:01:50,811
My reply starts with Done, Failed or Partial. Then come the numbers, the files and the code, so the adversary can run it again.
